                    <occupation>historian</occupation>
                    <occupation>politician</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Joseph Vallence Bevan was an Irish-American student of <persName key="OGI01">James Ogilvie</persName>. He asked Godwin to advise on a course of studies and 
      Godwin's subsequent advice was printed as <title>Letters of Advice to 
      a Young American</title> in 1818. The death of his father cut 
      short his stay in Britain. He was appointed official historian of the state of Georgia in 1824 and elected to the House of Representatives for Georgia in 1827.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="MS">MS Abinger c. 19, fol., 60; 19 March 1818</bibl>
